    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1698.535484372624,
        -412.2589752330893
      ],
      "size": [
        518.0563379670084,
        809.3852845441536
      ],
      "flags": {
        "collapsed": false
      },
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "👑 Pixaroma - Note - START HERE",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MODELS AND NODES USED IN THIS WORKFLOW  \n\n---\n\n### Models are downloaded automatically the first time you use the workflow.\n \n---\n\n## 🧩 Nodes Installed from Manager  \n\n- ComfyUI-Easy-Use\n- Qwen3-TTS - Voice Synthesis & Cloning\n- ComfyUI_LayerStyle\n\nRead More about Qwen TTS Node [HERE](https://github.com/flybirdxx/ComfyUI-Qwen-TTS)\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Resources  \n🎥 **Tutorials:** [Pixaroma YouTube Channel](https://www.youtube.com/@pixaroma)  \n💬 **Community Discord:** [Join Here](https://discord.com/invite/gggpkVgBf3)\n\n---\n\n## 🎭 Qwen3 Multi-Voice Dialogue Workflow (VoiceDesign + Dialogue)\n\nCreate multiple character voices, then generate a full dialogue scene as one audio file.\n\n### 🧠 What It Does\n- Builds **Character voices** using **VoiceDesign** + **Voice Direction**\n- Stores them in **RoleBank** (Character 1 = man, Character 2 = woman, etc.)\n- Generates a multi-speaker script using **DialogueInference**\n- Outputs a single MP3 (merged dialogue)\n\n### ✍️ How To Use\n1. **Character 1**\n   - **Speech Text**: short sample line for that character\n   - **Voice Direction**: describe the voice style (required for VoiceDesign)\n\n2. **Character 2**\n   - Same as Character 1 (different Speech Text + Voice Direction)\n\n3. **Add more characters**\n   - Duplicate a Character block and give it a new RoleBank name (`role_name_3`, `role_name_4`, etc.)\n\n4. **Dialogue**\n   - Write your script in this format (one line per speaker):\n     > role_name: dialogue text\n   - Example:\n     > man: Where are we going?  \n     > woman: Just trust me.\n\n5. Click **Run**\n\n### 💾 MP3 Save Location\n- Preview inside **Save Audio (MP3)**\n- Saves under: `ComfyUI\\output\\audio`"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
